Use the CSS **`:hover`** pseudo-class on the `span` itself; `:hover` applies when the pointer is over the element, and it works on all elements, not just links.[4][8]

```html
<span class="my-span">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.my-span {
  color: black;
}

.my-span:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If the `span` already has an inline `style="color: ..."` on it, that inline style can override your stylesheet, so remove the inline style or increase specificity if needed.[1][4]

```css
.parent .my-span:hover {
  color: red !important;
}
```

If you want the color change to animate smoothly, add a transition:[4]

```css
.my-span {
  color: black;
  transition: color 0.3s ease;
}

.my-span:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

